(*) In monster form, you get the very slow healing pace of one HP every
20 turns. A vampire lord has intrinsic regeneration, which turns this
into one HP per turn (which is good, but not as good as what a
non-polymorphed player naturallay gets towards the end of the game).
Regeneration costs one extra nutrition point every other turn. But a
vampire is not a "eating" monster (this does not prevent you from
actually eating) so he does not lose nutrition except for the
regeneration cost and the 1-in-20 cost of amulets and rings. Also, this
intrinsic slower digestion does not include protection from swallowing
monsters.


